<!-- A placeholder, and the answer to the note that used to sit here. Every route other than
     this one used to be served with a 404 status, so listing them would only have filled Search
     Console with missing-page reports. They are real files now: the deploy runs
     Duniverse.Prerender, which writes an index.html for every route and then rewrites this
     sitemap from the same walk, so the list that ships can never drift from the pages that
     actually exist. Sealed records are left out of it on purpose; their pages get written too,
     but they carry a noindex so their names stay off the open web.

     What is written here only matters if someone serves wwwroot straight from the repo without
     running the deploy, which is why it still names the one page that is always real. -->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://www.duniverse.org/</loc>
  </url>
</urlset>
